 5. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Shoshana Gordon/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 🎓 Multiple states are making bids to host the U.S. Space Academy.

 The big picture: Axios reporters John Frank and Ryan Deto covered pitches from Colorado Springs and Pittsburgh , respectively. Maryland and Virginia are also making moves, Axios' Mimi Montgomery reports. 💭 My thought bubble: It seems like nearly every state is making a pitch for Trump's Space Academy, but the question is whether the new Congress will ultimately provide funding. 📡 RBC Signals netted a $10 million strategic growth investment from Washington Harbour Partners, the firm announced today .

 Why it matters: Washington Harbour Partners has a wide range of space investments , from SpaceX to startups, and now it's eyeing the Redmond, Washington, data and satellite connectivity firm's tech. 💭 My thought bubble: I'll be chatting with Washington Harbour Partners CEO and founder Mina Faltas at the Axios Future of Defense Summit today to unpack this investment. 💥 Ursa Major and Avio USA netted a joint RTX contract to develop solid-rocket motors for the Tomahawk cruise missile, my colleague Colin reports.

 Why it matters: The work is expected to produce a pair of qualified booster vendors to support one of the most in-demand munitions in the U.S. inventory. 💭 Colin's thought bubble: "Few people have wielded the Tomahawk cruise missile like Commander in Chief Donald Trump. More Tomahawk contributors is a good thing for the U.S. and potential buyers." 
 
